1
00:00:03,753 --> 00:00:05,171
<i>You write something here first, boss.</i>

2
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:08,925
<i>- It should come from your heart.</i>
<i>- Boss, come on.</i>

3
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:12,887
<i>You write songs, don't you?</i>

4
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,474
<i>Maybe you can share your talent</i>
<i>when it comes to words.</i>

5
00:00:20,228 --> 00:00:22,814
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

6
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,941
[JORDAN] <i>We've known</i>
<i>each other for so long.</i>

7
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:26,818
<i>There are good times</i>

8
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:28,028
<i>and bad.</i>

9
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:30,321
<i>We've seen it all.</i>

10
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:34,034
<i>And I can't help</i>

11
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:36,369
<i>but admire how you rose above it.</i>

12
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,414
<i>I can't help</i>

13
00:00:39,497 --> 00:00:40,957
<i>but fall.</i>

14
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,917
<i>So let me take this chance to say…</i>

15
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:47,046
<i>I think I love you.</i>

16
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:51,926
<i>And if someday, life gets heavy,</i>

17
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:55,180
<i>or when the road is hard to see,</i>

18
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,725
<i>when your world is full of questions,</i>

19
00:01:00,018 --> 00:01:02,228
<i>you can always run to me.</i>

20
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:07,942
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

21
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:14,449
<i>Auntie…</i>

22
00:01:14,532 --> 00:01:17,994
<i>Can we invite Papa</i>
<i>to my moving-up ceremony?</i>

23
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:20,455
<i>I got high honors.</i>

24
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,374
[ENRICO] <i>Remember this, son.</i>

25
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:25,418
<i>From now on, I'll always be here for you.</i>

26
00:01:26,002 --> 00:01:28,546
[PRECIOUS]
<i>Don't get your hopes up too much.</i>

27
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:31,925
<i>Don't expect him to be allowed</i>
<i>to meet you all the time.</i>

28
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:37,096
[ENRICO] <i>You're right, Precious.</i>

29
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,723
<i>I deceived you.</i>

30
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:42,352
<i>But even though I wasn't honest with you,</i>

31
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:44,521
<i>the love I have for my children</i>

32
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:46,314
<i>and for you…</i>

33
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:49,317
<i>is real.</i>

34
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:54,364
[BILLY] <i>You got hurt. Are you all right?</i>

35
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:56,366
<i>I'm all right, Billy.</i>

36
00:01:56,449 --> 00:01:58,326
<i>But you have to look at this.</i>

37
00:02:03,039 --> 00:02:05,416
[BILLY] <i>So they've been keeping</i>
<i>an eye on me for a while now?</i>

38
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:09,504
<i>Auntie Pres, right from the start,</i>

39
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:11,714
<i>they've been planning this all along.</i>

40
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:15,009
<i>That's why we need to be more careful.</i>

41
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:18,096
<i>We don't know why they're going after you.</i>

42
00:02:18,179 --> 00:02:20,598
[MARIELA] <i>They're living lavishly.</i>

43
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:23,643
<i>They're living a luxurious life.</i>

44
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:28,690
<i>And now, they have your father too!</i>

45
00:02:28,773 --> 00:02:30,775
<i>While us?</i>

46
00:02:30,859 --> 00:02:34,737
[SOBS] <i>We've got nothing left!</i>

47
00:02:37,031 --> 00:02:41,995
<i>Now I understand why you're</i>
<i>so furious at that Billy!</i>

48
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:43,997
<i>I'll kill them!</i>

49
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,498
<i>I'll kill them both!</i>

50
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,125
<i>I'll kill them!</i>

51
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:49,168
- [BEA] <i>Ma! Ma!</i>
- [SOBBING]

52
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:50,795
<i>No one's dying.</i>

53
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:53,298
[SHUSHING]

54
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:56,050
<i>That's why, Ma, you have to promise me</i>

55
00:02:56,634 --> 00:03:02,223
<i>that you'll leave our revenge up to me.</i>

56
00:03:07,228 --> 00:03:09,314
[OLIVER] It's here, it's ready!

57
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:14,110
[OLIVER] Ta-da!

58
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:15,361
What's that?

59
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:19,073
Since you weren't able
to come to my birthday parties,

60
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:21,034
I'll just show them to you instead!

61
00:03:21,117 --> 00:03:23,870
This here is from my first birthday!

62
00:03:23,953 --> 00:03:25,705
It was at Auntie's house before.

63
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:28,291
This here is Jordan, Billy's best friend.

64
00:03:28,374 --> 00:03:29,918
Good buddies!

65
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:32,128
After that,

66
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:35,131
we started celebrating
my birthdays at the cemetery

67
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:38,259
so we could celebrate it with Mama.

68
00:03:38,843 --> 00:03:42,555
All of my birthdays are fun.

69
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:46,226
Except for when I turned seven.

70
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,853
Why? What happened when you turned seven?

71
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:50,396
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

72
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,065
I got rushed to the hospital.

73
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:55,443
That's when we found out
that I'm diabetic.

74
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:59,739
But, see, I'm really strong
and bounced back.

75
00:03:59,822 --> 00:04:03,076
I even won during Family Day.
Nailed it, huh?

76
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,412
I think Billy danced back then…

77
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:10,041
Like this, one, two, three, four, yeah!

78
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:12,418
Try to do it with me, Pa.
Three, two, one, go!

79
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:15,964
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

80
00:04:16,047 --> 00:04:17,590
- Let's go again.
- Is this right?

81
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:20,218
One, two, three, four, five, six!

82
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:21,803
- That was great!
- [LAUGHTER]

83
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:23,513
Wait, what about this?

84
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:26,724
[OLIVER] That was my last birthday.

85
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:28,810
You know,

86
00:04:28,893 --> 00:04:30,603
that birthday

87
00:04:31,479 --> 00:04:33,231
was both happy and sad.

88
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:36,067
Because it was my birthday,

89
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:39,112
but also the day Mom died.

90
00:04:39,195 --> 00:04:42,824
You know what happened to Mom, right?

91
00:04:42,907 --> 00:04:45,243
She died while giving birth to me.

92
00:04:45,326 --> 00:04:51,249
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:52,834
I'm sorry, Oliver.

94
00:04:52,917 --> 00:04:55,503
I'm sorry that I wasn't there
when you all needed me.

95
00:04:55,586 --> 00:04:57,380
When your mom needed me.

96
00:04:58,381 --> 00:04:59,465
[OLIVER] Pa,

97
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:01,301
did you ever love Mom?

98
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:08,599
You know what, Oliver?
I loved your mother.

99
00:05:08,683 --> 00:05:11,769
It's a shame that I didn't have the chance

100
00:05:11,853 --> 00:05:13,521
to ask for her forgiveness.

101
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:18,067
Billy always says that

102
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:21,112
Mom is watching over us from heaven.

103
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:25,408
I'm sure she can see how sorry you are.

104
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:32,165
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:05:32,248 --> 00:05:35,793
- Stay here, I'll get some water.
- [OLIVER] Here, Pa, look.

106
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:38,421
I look just like you.
We're both good-looking.

107
00:05:39,005 --> 00:05:41,049
[ENRICO] When did you
start wearing glasses?

108
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:42,133
I'm just like you.

109
00:05:42,216 --> 00:05:44,177
We're both wearing glasses. Both handsome.

110
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,094
Ha!

111
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:46,888
So you've always been copying me?

112
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:48,806
- Yes.
- What about him?

113
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:51,059
Is he courting your sister?

114
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:53,811
- No. They're just friends.
- Hmm? Really?

115
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:54,937
Promise.

116
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,230
- I promise.
- [CHUCKLES]

117
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:58,566
He needs to ask for
my permission first, okay?

118
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:00,318
- I promise. I promise.
- Is that okay?

119
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:07,116
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

120
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:45,988
Bye, Pa! I'll see you tomorrow.

121
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:49,992
Ask your sister
for her permission first, okay?

122
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:53,913
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:55,498
Thank you, Precious.

124
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:02,130
[OLIVER] I hope Billy
is with us next time.

125
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:03,923
Hug?

126
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:05,049
Hug. Hug.

127
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:07,051
- Fist bump.
- Fist bump.

128
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:08,511
[OLIVER] Fist bump!

129
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:10,221
- Boom.
- Boom. [CHUCKLES]

130
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:11,806
- Bye, Pa!
- Be good, okay?

131
00:07:11,889 --> 00:07:13,099
- Yes!
- Okay, go!

132
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:18,646
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:20,356
- [ENRICO] Take care!
- [CAR DOOR SLAMS]

134
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:33,578
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:07:35,371 --> 00:07:36,497
[GATE CREAKS]

136
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:55,266
[TENSE MUSIC FADES]

137
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:56,726
[BILLY] What are you wearing?

138
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,186
- What's wrong?
- Fix it.

139
00:07:58,269 --> 00:08:00,396
- You should've borrowed mine.
- What is that? You could've--

140
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,355
Hi, guys.

141
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:03,065
- Hi.
- Ready?

142
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,025
- Yes.
- Yes.

143
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:07,069
Just want to let you guys know that
I'm very excited about this partnership.

144
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:09,572
And also, just to formalize everything,

145
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:14,368
with this agreement, I acquired
the exclusive franchise right of LoveList

146
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:17,622
for the entire
North American region, right?

147
00:08:17,705 --> 00:08:19,707
- Exclusive territory.
- [PETER] All right.

148
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,334
But the brand ownership stays with us.

149
00:08:21,417 --> 00:08:23,586
- [PETER] Of course.
- That's part of our agreement. Yes.

150
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:26,339
And you guys will be operating
our global standards.

151
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:27,924
- [BILLY] Mm-hmm.
- Marketing templates.

152
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:31,135
Platform architecture.
Expansion strategies.

153
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:32,678
Yeah, but everything needs to be aligned.

154
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:35,181
Yes, of course.
I'm not here to change the brand.

155
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:37,642
- I'm just here to scale it.
- Perfect. Okay.

156
00:08:37,725 --> 00:08:40,937
As long as we protect
what makes LoveList LoveList.

157
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:41,896
Right.

158
00:08:41,979 --> 00:08:45,316
Well, thirty million
is a serious investment.

159
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:46,734
Yes, it is.

160
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:49,403
Thank you so much again for your trust.
We won't take it lightly.

161
00:08:49,487 --> 00:08:50,821
- [PETER] Right.
- Yes, thank you.

162
00:08:50,905 --> 00:08:52,240
- Shall we?
- Yes.

163
00:08:52,323 --> 00:08:54,325
- Yes, I think we're ready. Let's go?
- Of course.

164
00:08:54,408 --> 00:08:56,244
- Ms. Billy, it's ready.
- Perfect timing.

165
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:58,538
- Perfect.
- All right. Thank you.

166
00:08:58,621 --> 00:08:59,914
- Let's go.
- All right. Thank you.

167
00:08:59,997 --> 00:09:02,083
[BLAIRE] Okay, you go first. Let's go!

168
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:03,209
[REPORTER] Hi, sir!

169
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:05,002
[REPORTER] Turn here! Smile!

170
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:06,754
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

171
00:09:06,837 --> 00:09:08,548
- [BILLY] Go ahead.
- [PETER] Ah, thank you.

172
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:10,508
- Okay.
- [BILLY] Thank you.

173
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:11,717
[BLAIRE] Go upstairs.

174
00:09:12,260 --> 00:09:13,678
Hi. How are you?

175
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:15,846
[BLAIRE] Come on, everyone!

176
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,723
[PEOPLE CLAPPING, CHEERING]

177
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,517
Let's take a photo!

178
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:21,269
- Photo?
- Okay.

179
00:09:21,852 --> 00:09:26,607
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]
- [HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

180
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:27,692
[BLAIRE] Smile!

181
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:34,240
- Now, sir, you can have the mic.
- Ah, okay. Sure.

182
00:09:34,323 --> 00:09:35,324
Hello. Check?

183
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:37,827
Hi. To our press,

184
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:39,620
to our beloved journalists,

185
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:43,124
our social media influencers,
and reporters,

186
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:44,875
thank you so much for being here today

187
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:46,335
as we…

188
00:09:46,419 --> 00:09:47,503
as LoveList

189
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:51,215
goes from a regional brand
to a global brand.

190
00:09:51,966 --> 00:09:54,552
- [BLAIRE] Awesome! Whoo!
- Thank you!

191
00:09:54,635 --> 00:09:56,512
[PEOPLE CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

192
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:57,888
You may take your seats.

193
00:09:57,972 --> 00:09:59,140
I'm excited. Thank you.

194
00:09:59,223 --> 00:10:00,933
And we can sign the contract now.

195
00:10:01,017 --> 00:10:01,851
[PETER] All right.

196
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:06,564
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

197
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:30,296
- [UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS]

198
00:10:41,223 --> 00:10:47,063
[PEOPLE CLAPPING]

199
00:10:50,566 --> 00:10:56,113
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

200
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:59,659
[CAMERA SHUTTERS CLICK]

201
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:11,003
[CAMERA SHUTTERS CLICKING]

202
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:18,886
[UPBEAT MUSIC FADES]

203
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:30,439
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:11:50,918 --> 00:11:53,796
- [CRISELDA] <i>My God, I was panicking.</i>
- [BEA] <i>What's happening here?</i>

205
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,589
[CRISELDA]
<i>What if you'd actually killed her?</i>

206
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:57,758
<i>Ma! Wait a minute. What's happening here?</i>

207
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:59,927
<i>We should be the ones asking you that.</i>

208
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:01,929
<i>I'll let you sleep here</i>
<i>in my unit for tonight,</i>

209
00:12:02,012 --> 00:12:04,348
<i>but you should be gone by the morning!</i>

210
00:12:04,432 --> 00:12:07,601
<i>Wait, Ms. Criselda. Don't do this to us.</i>

211
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:09,687
<i>You haven't paid rent</i>
<i>for two months already!</i>

212
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:11,772
<i>If I'd only known that you were criminals,</i>

213
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,190
<i>I never would have let you live here!</i>

214
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:15,818
<i>They're living lavishly.</i>

215
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:21,073
[SOBS] <i>They have a beautiful house.</i>

216
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:24,160
<i>They're living a luxurious life.</i>

217
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:29,206
<i>And now, they have your father too!</i>

218
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:31,292
<i>While us?</i>

219
00:12:31,375 --> 00:12:35,254
[SOBS] <i>We've got nothing left!</i>

220
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:38,841
<i>Look at what we have, Bea!</i>

221
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:42,011
[CRIES] <i>Nothing!</i>

222
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:43,345
<i>Ma…</i>

223
00:12:43,429 --> 00:12:49,351
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:12,625
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

225
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:33,896
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

226
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:41,904
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

227
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:03,008
[MOROSE MUSIC
CONTINUES]

228
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:20,985
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

229
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:40,880
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

230
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:52,391
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:12,411
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

232
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:33,974
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:46,946
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

234
00:15:49,156 --> 00:15:51,325
- [ALL] Cheers!
- [GLASSES CLINKING]

235
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:52,660
- [MARJ] Whoo-hoo!
- [RALPH] Yeah!

236
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:55,037
- Congrats!
- [RALPH] Whoo!

237
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:59,792
[CHARM] Gosh, Billy,
the amount earlier was huge.

238
00:15:59,875 --> 00:16:01,585
- You can retire now.
- [GLASSES THUDDING]

239
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:03,921
What do you mean, retire? I wish.

240
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,756
As long as that mischievous kid
is still studying,

241
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:06,924
retirement isn't an option.

242
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:10,052
Come on. Oliver's smart, right?

243
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:12,304
He'll qualify for a scholarship.

244
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:14,640
- Just relax, girl.
- [CHARM] True.

245
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:16,392
How about

246
00:16:16,475 --> 00:16:18,227
- we go to the beach?
- [MARJ SQUEALING]

247
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:20,145
- Oh, that could work!
- [MARJ] Yes!

248
00:16:20,229 --> 00:16:22,481
Yes, Oliver really is smart.

249
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:26,527
But even if he gets into
the Kingsley scholarship program,

250
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,654
the daily expenses are no joke.

251
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:30,155
Unless you're willing to chip in.

252
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:31,532
You guys? Pitch in?

253
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:33,367
You know what? Let's do it.

254
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:35,369
When was your last beach trip?

255
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:39,039
Back before Oliver even learned to talk.

256
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:40,791
- That's it, right?
- You're so dramatic!

257
00:16:40,874 --> 00:16:42,084
- [CHARM] Yeah.
- Hey, come on.

258
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:46,588
Let's go to the beach so I can wear
the outfits I bought online!

259
00:16:46,672 --> 00:16:52,428
You know, I'm sure this will just end up
being just another daydream again.

260
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:56,140
Let's please make it happen
this time. Okay?

261
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:58,308
- Oh!
- I'm in!

262
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,643
- [CHARM] Let's go!
- [TONI] Right?

263
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,687
Hey, you're getting me drunk
just to get me to agree.

264
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:02,980
- You're so obvious.
- Huh? What?

265
00:17:03,063 --> 00:17:05,441
- Why just mine? Refill yours too!
- Fine!

266
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:07,693
- Well, just a suggestion.
- [SOFT THUD]

267
00:17:07,776 --> 00:17:09,862
Book that flight.
You know Billy's details.

268
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:11,196
- Come on.
- Yes! Yeah!

269
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,448
- Marj, go.
- [CLAPPING]

270
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:14,533
- Go, go, go, go! Yes!
- Seriously? Hey, don't!

271
00:17:14,616 --> 00:17:15,826
- We can't all go together--
- Go!

272
00:17:15,909 --> 00:17:17,327
- No, no, no, no!
- Relax, relax!

273
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:18,412
- We can't!
- Relax!

274
00:17:18,495 --> 00:17:20,122
- Oh, look at this.
- Why a boat?

275
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:21,457
Where are we going? Are you serious?

276
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:22,666
- [TONI] We'll handle it.
- Toni.

277
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,585
- [TONI] Just sit there.
- Where, where?

278
00:17:24,668 --> 00:17:26,545
No one's going to approve your leave!

279
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:28,505
- No, no! Just chill.
- [TONI] It's been a long time--

280
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:30,716
- Hey, don't!
- Let's talk about it for a sec.

281
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:33,635
- But have a drink first.
- I don't want to!

282
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:36,972
I don't want to drink!
You're tricking me.

283
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:39,183
Okay, let's drink together now!

284
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:41,351
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

285
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,520
- Let's go to the beach!
- Let's go!

286
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:45,314
[CHANTING] Let's go to the beach!

287
00:17:45,397 --> 00:17:47,024
- Let's go to the beach!
- [GLASSES CLINKING]

288
00:17:47,107 --> 00:17:49,443
- Let's go to the beach!
- When? When are we going?

289
00:17:49,526 --> 00:17:50,527
[BILLY GIGGLES]

290
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:53,280
[MUSIC TURNS STIRRING]

291
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:55,741
[PETER] Why? What are you looking at?

292
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:56,825
[MAN] There's a lady there.

293
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,410
Um…

294
00:18:00,954 --> 00:18:02,915
- [PETER] Is she pretty?
- [MAN] Of course.

295
00:18:02,998 --> 00:18:05,334
All right. Just show her to me.

296
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:12,299
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:18:15,427 --> 00:18:16,637
I'll buy one.

298
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:29,733
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

299
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:31,026
Thanks.

300
00:18:44,832 --> 00:18:47,918
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

301
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:49,962
One, please.

302
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:59,888
[RACY MUSIC PLAYING]

303
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:01,056
[BEA] It's so hot.

304
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:03,350
So hot.

305
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:05,269
It's so hot in here.

306
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:09,523
It really is.

307
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:12,651
[BEA SIGHS]

308
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:17,906
So, you believe in online dating?

309
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:19,032
Hmm?

310
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:22,744
[BEA HALF-LAUGHS] I guess.

311
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:25,330
That's why I'm using this app.

312
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:27,082
[RACY MUSIC CONTINUES]

313
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,417
Is it any good?

314
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,128
I hope so.

315
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:33,714
Let's see.

316
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:38,552
I hope I can find

317
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:39,720
my match.

318
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:46,310
I can't believe you're single.

319
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:48,812
Yes.

320
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:49,855
I'm single.

321
00:19:49,938 --> 00:19:51,356
- Mm-hmm.
- Super single.

322
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:52,274
And you?

323
00:19:53,525 --> 00:19:54,401
Yeah.

324
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:55,861
Yeah.

325
00:19:55,944 --> 00:19:57,029
No, I'm single.

326
00:19:57,613 --> 00:19:58,614
Oh!

327
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:01,867
- You're single too?
- Mm-hmm.

328
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:03,660
[RACY MUSIC CONTINUES]

329
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:04,953
Mm!

330
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,833
So that means

331
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:14,796
I don't need this app anymore.

332
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:18,967
Ooh, you're a feisty one, I see.

333
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:20,219
- [BEA] Mm?
- Mm.

334
00:20:21,428 --> 00:20:23,513
As the saying goes,

335
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:24,848
"Life is short."

336
00:20:26,141 --> 00:20:28,143
So if you want something,

337
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:31,939
you should get it.

338
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:35,359
Get it?

339
00:20:35,442 --> 00:20:37,778
Oh, I get it.

340
00:20:37,861 --> 00:20:39,529
You get it?

341
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:41,907
Mm-hmm.

342
00:20:41,990 --> 00:20:44,034
[BEA GIGGLES]

343
00:20:44,117 --> 00:20:45,410
Bea.

344
00:20:45,494 --> 00:20:46,411
Peter.

345
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:48,664
Peter.

346
00:20:48,747 --> 00:20:55,754
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

347
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:02,970
[BAND PLAYING]

348
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:05,639
[JORDAN SINGING]
<i>♪ Why is it like that? ♪</i>

349
00:21:05,722 --> 00:21:07,516
<i>♪ So many are… ♪</i>

350
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:09,518
[VALERIE] <i>Maybe I was</i>
<i>hoping eventually,</i>

351
00:21:09,601 --> 00:21:11,311
<i>you'll learn to love me more</i>
<i>than you love her.</i>

352
00:21:12,729 --> 00:21:14,398
<i>But what's written there is true.</i>

353
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:17,150
<i>But you didn't write this</i>
<i>to express Robbie's feelings for me.</i>

354
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:18,443
<i>What's holding you back?</i>

355
00:21:18,527 --> 00:21:20,112
<i>Why can't you just be</i>
<i>honest with her?</i>

356
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:21,363
<i>Thank you.</i>

357
00:21:22,197 --> 00:21:25,409
[PRECIOUS] <i>Your father said</i>
<i>he'll never leave you guys again.</i>

358
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:26,576
<i>That will be the end of it.</i>

359
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:27,953
This is going to hurt Oliver.

360
00:21:28,036 --> 00:21:31,581
<i>Is it just Oliver who will get hurt?</i>
<i>Or you too?</i>

361
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:34,376
<i>Giving you a chance</i>
<i>was already a huge ask.</i>

362
00:21:34,459 --> 00:21:35,961
<i>Please. I need more</i>
<i>time with him.</i>

363
00:21:36,044 --> 00:21:37,337
<i>I'll deal with them.</i>

364
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:39,256
<i>Billy is going down.</i>

365
00:21:39,339 --> 00:21:44,094
[MARIELA] <i>As long as your father</i>
<i>and his mistress are together,</i>

366
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:47,139
<i>I will never be okay.</i>

367
00:21:47,222 --> 00:21:50,017
<i>Mariela, please.</i>
<i>Leave us alone.</i>

368
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:52,477
<i>If it had happened to you,</i>
<i>you'd be angry too.</i>

369
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:54,730
<i>What's your real problem</i>
<i>with me and my daughter?</i>

370
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:56,356
[MARIELA]
<i>This should've been ours.</i>

371
00:21:56,440 --> 00:22:01,278
<i>So we won't stop</i>
<i>until we get what is rightfully ours!</i>
